{"role":"user","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<user_query>\nCreate a single-file Japanese mahjong game at `index.html` in the user's workspace. If workspace path is unknown, use a sensible path: create the file under `C:\\Users\\Keigo\\.cursor\\projects\\empty-window\\index.html` or the current workspace root if it exists.\n\nRequirements (must all be satisfied):\n\n**Tech**: HTML5, CSS3, Vanilla JavaScript only. No external assets. Tiles MUST be Unicode mahjong characters (🀇-🀏, 🀐-🀘, 🀙-🀡, 🀀🀁🀂🀃🀄🀅🀆).\n\n**Players**: 4-player: human (bottom) vs 3 CPUs. CPU turns: add ~500ms delay before discard so it feels like playing.\n\n**Deck**: 136 tiles — man/pin/sou 1-9 ×4 each, winds ESWN and dragons 白發中 ×4 each.\n\n**Rules simplified**:\n- No pon/chi/kan (no calls). Closed hand only.\n- Turn flow: draw (current player goes 13→14), optional win (tsumo if 14 completes), optional riichi if applicable, discard to river, then next player. Human clicks tile to discard.\n- **Ron**: If an opponent discards a tile that completes the human's 13-tile hand (human has 13, discard is the 14th), show prominent Ron opportunity — auto-popup or large button \"ロン！\" and resolve win.\n- **Riichi**: Implement a \"リーチ\" button when the human is tenpai (13 tiles that can win on some tile(s)); after riichi, enforce simplified lock: only allow discarding the drawn tile (standard furiten not required unless easy).\n- **Yaku-optional**: Winning = standard 4 groups + 1 pair (groups can be 順子 or 刻子; numbered tiles allow sequences; honors only triplets). No yaku check — any valid standard form wins.\n- **Win detection**: When 14 tiles form valid hand, show large \"アガリ（勝利）！\" overlay/message.\n\n**UI/UX for beginners (Japanese text)**:\n- Clear navigation: show whose turn (自分の番 / CPUの番 + seat name).\n- Message area: always tells what to do next (ツモしました、捨てる牌を選んでください、相手の番です、など).\n- **Hint**: Highlight a suggested discard tile (heuristic: e.g. discard that maximizes flexibility / or simple \"furthest from completing melds\" — document in comments; must be helpful not random).\n- Hand sorted (理牌) always; drawn tile visually separated to the right (slightly apart).\n- Layout: center = main river / discard piles for all; own hand bottom; opponent discards top/left/right as specified.\n\n**CPU AI**: Simple but not instant — after delay, discard a reasonable tile (not always random; avoid breaking pairs if possible, simple scoring).\n\n**Code quality**: Extensive Japanese comments explaining each section. One HTML file with embedded CSS and JS.\n\n**Do not** use canvas libraries or images. Unicode only for tiles.\n\nAfter writing, verify the file exists and is self-contained.\n\nReturn: path to index.html and brief note on how to open it.\n</user_query>"}]}}
